From: juniorverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: denali-lcd: match the ten-core boot topology

The LCD Surface Pro 11 with X1P64100 exposes ten enabled CPUs in its
Windows MADT. GICC UID 7 (MPIDR 0x10300) and UID 11 (MPIDR 0x20300)
have the enabled flag clear. Remove those CPU nodes, their cpu-map
entries and their PSCI CPU power domains from the LCD board. Keep
all three cluster and SCMI performance domains for the remaining CPUs.

Also remove the system power domain's SS3 idle-state reference, while
retaining CPU C4 and cluster CL4/CL5. This carries the existing D20
boot-parity configuration into the packaged LCD DTB; it does not claim
that SS3 caused the earlier reset. The M5 GPU-off boot used this
configuration and reached GNOME, whereas the GPU-on boot reset at
session start. SS3 can be reconsidered with a separate device test.

The MADT is sources/windows/live-inventory/acpi/apic.dat, SHA-256
50b032d657ad12b06793d4de71f0425d93a143fbf45965645203b40009a038d0.
The GICC records start at 0x25c and 0x39c; their flags are at 0x268
and 0x3a8, and MPIDRs at 0x2a0 and 0x3e0, respectively.

Limit the change to the LCD board and preserve the separately applied
speaker and GPU disablement. Device variant builders using this series
must omit the legacy parity deletions: inherit the patched board once.

Assisted-by: Codex gpt-6.1-sol
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
@@ -9,6 +9,11 @@
 
 #include "hamoa.dtsi"
 #include "x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi"
+
+/delete-node/ &cpu7;
+/delete-node/ &cpu11;
+/delete-node/ &cpu_pd7;
+/delete-node/ &cpu_pd11;
 
 &{/sound} {
 	status = "disabled";
@@ -83,6 +88,14 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&{/cpus/cpu-map/cluster1} {
+	/delete-node/ core3;
+};
+
+&cpu_map_cluster2 {
+	/delete-node/ core3;
+};
+
 &gpi_dma1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
@@ -108,6 +121,10 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&system_pd {
+	/delete-property/ domain-idle-states;
+};
+
 &tlmm {
 	qup_spi10_data23: qup-spi10-data23-state {
 		pins = "gpio49", "gpio50";
